## 14. Flag, deployment, rollback, activation

- Flag `rme.doctor_performed_treatments` (`FEATURE_RME_DOCTOR_PERFORMED_TREATMENTS`), default **OFF**, risk high,
  captured at config build (rule 92). While off: routes 404 for an authorized doctor (route middleware runs first,
  so an account without `complete_rme_examination` gets 403 and a roomless visit redirects — the same order as every
  RME route), service refuses `DPT_NOT_ENABLED`, RME page and cashier pages render as before, rule 218 snapshot v1.
  The two read-only oversight counts render regardless and read 0 (rule 218 §9 precedent) — no data, no write.
- Deploy: `php artisan migrate --force` (one additive migration). No seeder, no permission, no role change.
- Rollback: flag OFF + config cache rebuild as the runtime user. Rows stay (clinical evidence, never dropped);
  `down()` refuses while rows exist.
- Activation = `ACTIVATION-RME-DOCTOR-PERFORMED-TREATMENTS-1`, a separate owner decision (DPT-Q8), independent of
  `rme.zero_value_closure` (also OFF).
- Status: `TECHNICAL_ENFORCEMENT_DEPLOYED_FLAG_OFF` — runtime `931c716c` (tree `150679aa`, PR #581) deployed
  2026-11-01 14:28 UTC (22:28 WITA), production-verified, GO tag `feature-rme-doctor-performed-treatments-1-implementation-go`
  (evidence: sprint record §8). The flag stays OFF.
- MEDIUM-1 (rule 218 §8) stays `PARTIALLY_MITIGATED`: the authoritative source now EXISTS but is OFF, optional,
  and detective. Never claim it closed.
